Production deployment for HEMA Squire — a single Hetzner CX23 running the app,
Caddy and Litestream under docker compose. The reasoning behind that shape is in
openspec/changes/add-deployment/design.md; the operational steps are in tasks.md
of the same directory.

Files
  Dockerfile          three stages: frontend build, backend, Caddy with the SPA
  docker-compose.yml  app + web + litestream; only `app` sees the full .env
  Caddyfile           TLS, SPA fallback, /api/* proxied
  litestream.yml      continuous WAL replication, 28-day retention
  cloud-init.yaml     host bootstrap (SSH hardening, Docker, unattended upgrades)
  deploy.sh           git pull && docker compose up -d --build, over SSH;
                      brings up litestream only when .env names a replica
  restore.sh          restore from the replica (drill and real recovery)
  .env.example        every variable; the filled copy also lives in a password
                      manager, because a new host needs it to come up
  secrets/            service-account JSON for the Sheets export; may be empty

Restore drill log
  A restore is a hypothesis until it has been performed on a machine other than
  production. Record each drill here, and repeat it when the stack changes
  materially (Litestream version, storage provider, database layout).

  date        performed by   restored to   result
